      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. the insurance angle is smart. \n\nbut i'm worried they'll just look at the report and say \"see, we're secure, we don't need to spend more.\" if they point out that there weren't actually any vulnerabilities found in this round, how do we respond to that without sounding like we're just trying to push a product? is there a way to suggest they have specific, uncaptured risks without actually claiming we found them?",
